{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall fill.</b> This word is anomalous in the holy tongue, for the sense of ומלאו is that the houses were full of them. Now we find \"מלאו ארבעה כדים מים\" (1 Kings 18:34), which is a transitive verb, as though it were written with patach in the mem and a dagesh in the lamed from the dagesh-building." "<b>And he turned.</b> R. Yeshuah said: ויפן means he turned back to Moses, for he was showing honor to royalty, that one turns toward the king when leaving and walks backward. Yefet said: when he finished his need and so forth — ופנית בבקר (Deuteronomy 16:7). Now what will one do with the word ויפן כה וכה (above, 2:12)? The sense of ויפן is from the root פנים, as though it were וירא, and behold Moses left from Pharaoh's presence without his permission. Scripture mentioned this because Pharaoh was angry and commanded to drive them out after they had been sent back."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:11.454854719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}